# Component Patterns

> Size limits, fetch rules, anti-patterns: `docs/PRODUCTION_STANDARDS.md` §4.

## Server vs Client
- Default to Server Components. Only add "use client" when the component needs:
  useState, useEffect, event handlers, browser APIs, or client-side hooks.
- Data fetching happens in Server Components or page.tsx via `lib/queries/*` — **not** `useEffect` + `fetch` for primary content.
- Client files: target ≤ 300 lines; split before 400. Do not add new god components.

## Client mutations
- Always check `res.ok` after `fetch`; show toast on error.
- On success: `startTransition(() => router.refresh())` to reload RSC data.
- Never call deleted API paths — notes use `POST /api/notes` with `parentType` + `parentId`.

## Props
- Props interface named `{ComponentName}Props`. Define above the component.
- Destructure props in the function signature.

## App shell layout
- New authenticated pages: prefer `<PageContainer width="wide" | "narrow" spacing="…">` from `@/components/shared/page-container` — it composes max-width with vertical rhythm.
- Existing pages may still use the lower-level `<AppContent variant="narrow" | "wide">` — both compose; do not add a separate `max-w-*` on the inner root.
- For full conventions on dashboard surfaces (primitives catalog, gating, charts theme, motion vocabulary) see `.cursor/rules/dashboard.mdc`.

## Styling
- Use shadcn/ui primitives from `@/components/ui/*` — never build custom buttons, inputs, dialogs from scratch.
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes.
- Never inline styles. Always use Tailwind classes.
- Framer Motion for animations. Keep animations subtle (200-300ms, ease-out).

## UI States
- Loading states: Use Skeleton components.
- Empty states: Use the shared EmptyState component with icon, title, and action.
- Error states: Catch and display user-friendly messages.

## Pro Features
- Wrap Pro-only UI in `<ProGate planTier={…} role={…} feature="…">` from `@/components/upgrade/pro-gate`. Its default fallback is the editorial `<ProUpsellCard>`.
- Use feature-level helpers in `@/lib/feature-flags` (`canSeeFullWrapped`, `canSeeAdvancedAnalytics`, …) rather than calling `hasProProductAccess` directly.
- Never hide Pro features entirely — show them gated with a calm upgrade prompt.

## Data Display
- Use `formatDate()` from `@/lib/utils` for dates.
- Numbers: use Intl.NumberFormat for locale-aware formatting.
